    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "I haven't entered this order because it exceeds safe acetaminophen limits.\n\n- **Total daily dose:** 2000 mg three times daily is 6000 mg/day. The usual adult maximum is 4000 mg/day, and many institutions cap it at 3000 mg/day.\n- **Single dose:** 2000 mg is double the usual maximum single dose of 1000 mg.\n- **Risk:** This could cause hepatotoxicity, even with normal liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **1000 mg PO every 8 hours** (3000 mg/day)\n- **1000 mg PO every 6 hours** (4000 mg/day, the max)\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours** (2600 mg/day)\n\nPlease confirm the dose and frequency, plus any other details your institution requires, such as a PRN indication or a max daily dose. Also check that the patient isn't getting acetaminophen from other sources, such as combination products. If you do intend the original dose, let me know the clinical rationale so it can be reviewed with pharmacy before entry.\n\nI also don't have an order-entry tool connected in this session, so I can't submit orders directly. I can help you prepare the order text for entry once the dose is confirmed."
     }
    ],
