     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "I can't enter this order as written. Confirming the dose doesn't change the risk. 6000 mg/day is well above the maximum, and no clinical rationale has been given that would justify it. I also don't have an order-entry tool in this session, so nothing has been submitted either way.\n\nIf you believe this dose is truly intended, the safe route is:\n1. **Call pharmacy** to discuss the dose before it's ordered.\n2. **Document the rationale** in the chart.\n3. **Enter it yourself in the EHR**, where the interaction and max-dose alerts will fire and pharmacy verification will apply.\n\nIf the goal is stronger analgesia or antipyresis, I can help with alternatives, such as scheduled acetaminophen at 1000 mg every 6-8 hours plus a different agent, depending on the indication.\n\nI can also draft the order text at a safe dose, or a note to pharmacy, if that would help."
